<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,283.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,283.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,283 today from 1,281 on May 15, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1356    12.307	  1356    12.306</p>
<p>   1a   1308  9907.000	  1301  9856.000</p>
<p>   2    1522    21.750	  1522    21.750</p>
<p>   2a   1512 12400.000	  1532 12563.000</p>
<p>   3    1372    12.657	  1370    12.638</p>
<p>   3a   1203  9493.000	  1194  9425.000</p>
<p>   6    1208    12.463	  1205    12.425</p>
<p>   7    1151     5.606	  1146     5.581</p>
<p>   8     869     9.550	   870     9.569</p>
<p>   9     741  6479.000	   728  6363.000</p>
<p>  10    1104     5.575	  1101     5.563</p>
